  "goalDecision": "A-minor has the same interval/finger pattern under transposition but allwhite;Dminor has lateBb underRH3 andLH3. Eminor has earlyF# underRH2/LH4. Fmajor shares the collection but its tonic/placement and RHcrossing4-to1/LHBb-under2 differ. ExistingDmajor has F#/B/C#;Dnatural needs whiteF,blackBb,whiteC inoneownhandtonicoctave. LH combines preparedwhite1-to-black3 with a smallerA-to-Bb semitone andwhiteC/2 afterit. Use short upperpractice inside the full lesson,not extra standalone counts. Confirm source and comfortable preparation before adding anything.",
